WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.620
Welcome to Grade 1 English, Unit 7: Let's Go!

2
00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:07.160
In this unit you will learn how we travel and get around.

3
00:00:07.660 --> 00:00:09.660
You will meet the words for ways to travel.

4
00:00:10.260 --> 00:00:13.120
They are walk, bus, car, bicycle and boat.

5
00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:15.560
You will learn to say how you go to school.

6
00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:17.120
You will talk about journeys.

7
00:00:17.760 --> 00:00:22.480
You will go somewhere with the people
you love, stay safe, and enjoy the trip.

8
00:00:23.280 --> 00:00:24.280
Say the words out loud.

9
00:00:24.900 --> 00:00:28.380
This is about confident everyday
English, not perfect spelling.

10
00:00:28.840 --> 00:00:34.260
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

11
00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:42.080
By the end of this unit, you will be able to name common
ways to travel (walk, bus, car, bicycle, boat, train, plane).

12
00:00:43.120 --> 00:00:47.780
You will also say how you get to
school: “I go to school by ___.”

13
00:00:48.540 --> 00:00:53.840
You will also say the action words for
travel (drive, ride, fly, float, walk).

14
00:00:54.940 --> 00:00:56.620
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

15
00:00:57.280 --> 00:01:03.080
Your vocabulary work begins with these
words: long, sing, ring, king, song, thin.

16
00:01:03.900 --> 00:01:08.260
Listen to each word, look at what it means,
and try to use it when you talk and write.

17
00:01:08.980 --> 00:01:13.460
The reading sequence includes Amal's
Big Bus Ride and Talk about Let's Go!.

18
00:01:14.400 --> 00:01:19.060
Read slowly, look at the pictures,
and find the big idea in each text.

19
00:01:19.640 --> 00:01:23.040
When you answer a question, point to the words that show it.

20
00:01:23.510 --> 00:01:26.660
The first language focus is Say how you travel.

21
00:01:27.220 --> 00:01:29.240
Tell us how you get to school each morning.

22
00:01:29.800 --> 00:01:32.150
Say the way you travel after the word 'by'.

23
00:01:32.640 --> 00:01:36.060
Look at the examples, then try
the pattern in your own sentences.

24
00:01:36.900 --> 00:01:40.500
In speaking, you will complete Speaking 1 - Listen and point.

25
00:01:41.380 --> 00:01:43.720
Say your ideas clearly and listen to your partner.

26
00:01:44.400 --> 00:01:49.940
In writing, you will draw, trace, copy or write,
then check your work with a grown-up or the AI tutor.

27
00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:51.700
You are ready to begin.

28
00:01:52.460 --> 00:01:57.880
Start with the words, then the reading and the
questions, then the grammar, speaking and writing.

29
00:01:58.680 --> 00:02:04.120
Ask the AI tutor for help any time, and bring your
questions to a live session too if you join one.
